Time Complexity:
----------------

Time complexity describes how the running time of an algorithm grows as the input size (n) increases.

It does not measure the actual time in seconds. Instead, it measures the number of basic operations an algorithm performs.

Example 1: Constant Time – O(1)

arr = [10, 20, 30, 40]
print(arr[2])

No matter how large the array is, accessing an element by index takes the same amount of work.

Time Complexity: O(1)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Example 2: Linear Time – O(n)

arr = [10, 20, 30, 40]

for num in arr:
    print(num)

If there are n elements, the loop runs n times.

Time Complexity: O(n)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Example 3: Quadratic Time – O(n²)

arr = [1, 2, 3]

for i in arr:
    for j in arr:
        print(i, j)

Each element is paired with every other element.

For n elements, operations = n × n.

Time Complexity: O(n²)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
